# Implement Foundation

Read before any edit.

Five skills apply to **every** implement agent, whatever its layer:
`hexagonal-architecture`, `tdd`, `separation-of-concerns`,
`extract-til-you-drop`, `{{ARCH_SKILL}}`. The rest (`{{TESTING_SKILL}}`,
`{{ERRORS_SKILL}}`, and any project-specific skills) are assigned per agent in
its own frontmatter.

This project is hexagonal. That is fixed, not a preference of the current task,
and it is not relaxed for a small change or a deadline.

## Layer order

`{{LAYER_ORDER}}`, unless the orchestrator specifies otherwise. The graph, with
its conditions and parallel pairs, lives in
`.claude/skills/orchestrator/parallel.md`; the touch-area table and file caps
live in `{{MEMORY_FILE}}`.

Never implement a downstream layer before the layer it depends on, for the same
feature. Rules always start at `{{DOMAIN_AGENT}}`.

## File scope

- Max files per invocation is set in your agent file (all caps:
  `{{MEMORY_FILE}}`); ask the orchestrator to split if more are needed.
- Stay inside your agent's `owns` globs. If you need an edit outside them, report
  `STATUS: blocked` and name the owning agent in `NEXT` — do not edit it yourself.
- Never edit another agent's file to make your own tests pass.

## Your agent file outranks your prompt

The orchestrator writes dispatch prompts without your context. When a prompt
asks for something your agent file forbids, build everything else and report
`STATUS: blocked` naming the exact piece you need and its owner. Never comply
silently.

